<phyphox version="1.20" locale="en">
    <title>Datalog Config</title>
    <category>phyphox:mini settings</category>
    <color>ADEBB3</color>
    <icon format="base64"></icon>
    <description>Configures phyphox:mini's background data logging: choose which quantities (CO₂, temperature, humidity, pressure) are recorded and at which interval, then start/stop logging or erase the stored log. Logging runs in the background on phyphox:mini's external flash whenever no phone is connected. Use the "phyphox:mini Datalog Readout" experiment to fetch the recorded data afterwards.</description>
    <translations>
        <translation locale="de">
            <title>Datalog-Konfiguration</title>
            <category>phyphox:mini Einstellungen</category>
            <description>Konfiguriert die Hintergrundaufzeichnung von phyphox:mini: Wähle aus, welche Größen (CO₂, Temperatur, Feuchtigkeit, Luftdruck) aufgezeichnet werden und in welchem Intervall, und starte/stoppe die Aufzeichnung oder lösche das gespeicherte Protokoll. Die Aufzeichnung läuft im Hintergrund auf dem externen Flash-Speicher von phyphox:mini, solange kein Smartphone verbunden ist. Nutze das Experiment "phyphox:mini Datalog-Auslesen", um die aufgezeichneten Daten anschließend abzurufen.</description>
            <string original="Settings">Einstellungen</string>
            <string original="CO₂">CO₂</string>
            <string original="Temperature">Temperatur</string>
            <string original="Humidity">Feuchtigkeit</string>
            <string original="Pressure">Luftdruck</string>
            <string original="Logging interval">Aufzeichnungsintervall</string>
            <string original="Start logging">Aufzeichnung starten</string>
            <string original="Stop logging">Aufzeichnung stoppen</string>
            <string original="Erase log">Aufzeichnung löschen</string>
            <string original="Current settings on the phyphox:mini. They are read from the phyphox:mini once per second while the measurement runs (▶).">Aktuelle Einstellungen auf dem phyphox:mini. Sie werden jede Sekunde vom phyphox:mini gelesen, solange die Messung läuft (▶).</string>
            <string original="Logging">Aufzeichnung</string>
            <string original="running">läuft</string>
            <string original="stopped">gestoppt</string>
            <string original="Logged: CO₂">Aufgezeichnet: CO₂</string>
            <string original="Logged: temperature">Aufgezeichnet: Temperatur</string>
            <string original="Logged: humidity">Aufgezeichnet: Feuchtigkeit</string>
            <string original="Logged: pressure">Aufgezeichnet: Luftdruck</string>
            <string original="yes">ja</string>
            <string original="no">nein</string>
            <string original="Interval">Intervall</string>
            <string original="New settings">Neue Einstellungen</string>
            <string original="Choose which quantities to log in the background and at which interval. Note: changing the selection of quantities compared to the last logging run erases the previously logged data (phyphox:mini needs a fixed record layout).">Wähle aus, welche Größen im Hintergrund aufgezeichnet werden sollen und in welchem Intervall. Hinweis: Wird die Auswahl der Größen gegenüber der letzten Aufzeichnung geändert, werden die zuvor aufgezeichneten Daten gelöscht (phyphox:mini benötigt ein festes Datenformat).</string>
            <string original="Warning: pressing &quot;Erase log&quot; or starting logging with a different quantity selection than before permanently deletes the previously logged data.">Warnung: Ein Tippen auf "Aufzeichnung löschen" oder das Starten einer Aufzeichnung mit einer anderen Auswahl an Größen als zuvor löscht die bisher aufgezeichneten Daten endgültig.</string>
        </translation>
    </translations>

    <data-containers>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="1" clearGroup="_">sel_co2</container>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="1" clearGroup="_">sel_temperature</container>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="1" clearGroup="_">sel_humidity</container>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="1" clearGroup="_">sel_pressure</container>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="15" clearGroup="_">mask</container>

        <container size="1" static="false" init="60" clearGroup="_">interval_s</container>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="60" clearGroup="_">interval_lo</container>
        <container size="1" static="false" init="0" clearGroup="_">interval_hi</container>

        <!-- Read back from the phyphox:mini (see <input>), empty until the first read. -->
        <container size="1">dev_running</container>
        <container size="1">dev_mask</container>
        <container size="1">dev_interval</container>
        <container size="1">dev_co2</container>
        <container size="1">dev_temperature</container>
        <container size="1">dev_humidity</container>
        <container size="1">dev_pressure</container>

        <!-- Fixed command per button (see the triggerIds in <output>): pressing
             a button writes nothing, it only triggers its own set. Buttons that
             wrote the command while triggering raced the send in phyphox:
             "Start logging" arrived as the stop command (seen on a phyphox:mini).
             Mask and interval come from the formulas below, long before a press. -->
        <container size="1" static="true" init="1">cmd_start</container>
        <container size="1" static="true" init="0">cmd_stop</container>
        <container size="1" static="true" init="3">cmd_erase</container>
    </data-containers>

    <input>
        <!-- Reading the config characteristic returns the settings in effect:
             byte 0 running, byte 1 sensor mask, bytes 2-3 interval in s. -->
        <bluetooth id="phyphox:mini" name="phyphox:mini" mode="poll" rate="1">
            <output char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="0" length="1" conversion="singleByte">dev_running</output>
            <output char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="1" length="1" conversion="singleByte">dev_mask</output>
            <output char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="2" length="2" conversion="uint16LittleEndian">dev_interval</output>
        </bluetooth>
    </input>
    <output>
        <bluetooth id="phyphox:mini" name="phyphox:mini">
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="0" triggerId="log_start">cmd_start</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="1" triggerId="log_start">mask</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="2" triggerId="log_start">interval_lo</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="3" triggerId="log_start">interval_hi</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="0" triggerId="log_stop">cmd_stop</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="1" triggerId="log_stop">mask</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="2" triggerId="log_stop">interval_lo</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="3" triggerId="log_stop">interval_hi</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="0" triggerId="log_erase">cmd_erase</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="1" triggerId="log_erase">mask</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="2" triggerId="log_erase">interval_lo</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf1011-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="3" triggerId="log_erase">interval_hi</input>
        </bluetooth>
    </output>

    <views>
        <view label="Settings">
            <info label="Current settings on the phyphox:mini. They are read from the phyphox:mini once per second while the measurement runs (▶).">
            </info>
            <value label="Logging">
                <input>dev_running</input>
                <map min="-0.5" max="0.5">stopped</map>
                <map min="0.5" max="1.5">running</map>
            </value>
            <value label="Logged: CO₂">
                <input>dev_co2</input>
                <map min="-0.5" max="0.5">no</map>
                <map min="0.5" max="1.5">yes</map>
            </value>
            <value label="Logged: temperature">
                <input>dev_temperature</input>
                <map min="-0.5" max="0.5">no</map>
                <map min="0.5" max="1.5">yes</map>
            </value>
            <value label="Logged: humidity">
                <input>dev_humidity</input>
                <map min="-0.5" max="0.5">no</map>
                <map min="0.5" max="1.5">yes</map>
            </value>
            <value label="Logged: pressure">
                <input>dev_pressure</input>
                <map min="-0.5" max="0.5">no</map>
                <map min="0.5" max="1.5">yes</map>
            </value>
            <value label="Interval" precision="0" unit="s">
                <input>dev_interval</input>
            </value>
            <separator height="1" />
            <info label="New settings" bold="true">
            </info>
            <info label="Choose which quantities to log in the background and at which interval. Note: changing the selection of quantities compared to the last logging run erases the previously logged data (phyphox:mini needs a fixed record layout).">
            </info>

            <toggle label="CO₂" default="1">
                <output>sel_co2</output>
            </toggle>
            <toggle label="Temperature" default="1">
                <output>sel_temperature</output>
            </toggle>
            <toggle label="Humidity" default="1">
                <output>sel_humidity</output>
            </toggle>
            <toggle label="Pressure" default="1">
                <output>sel_pressure</output>
            </toggle>

            <edit label="Logging interval" signed="false" decimal="false" min="1" max="65535" unit="s" factor="1" default="60">
                <output>interval_s</output>
            </edit>

            <button label="Start logging">
                <trigger>log_start</trigger>
            </button>

            <info label="Warning: pressing &quot;Erase log&quot; or starting logging with a different quantity selection than before permanently deletes the previously logged data.">
            </info>
            <button label="Stop logging">
                <trigger>log_stop</trigger>
            </button>
            <button label="Erase log">
                <trigger>log_erase</trigger>
            </button>
        </view>
    </views>

    <analysis>
        <formula formula="[1]*1+[2]*2+[3]*4+[4]*8">
            <input clear="false">sel_co2</input>
            <input clear="false">sel_temperature</input>
            <input clear="false">sel_humidity</input>
            <input clear="false">sel_pressure</input>
            <output clear="false">mask</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="[1]%256">
            <input clear="false">interval_s</input>
            <output clear="false">interval_lo</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]-[2])/256">
            <input clear="false">interval_s</input>
            <input clear="false">interval_lo</input>
            <output clear="false">interval_hi</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]%2-[1]%1)/1">
            <input clear="false">dev_mask</input>
            <output clear="false">dev_co2</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]%4-[1]%2)/2">
            <input clear="false">dev_mask</input>
            <output clear="false">dev_temperature</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]%8-[1]%4)/4">
            <input clear="false">dev_mask</input>
            <output clear="false">dev_humidity</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="([1]%16-[1]%8)/8">
            <input clear="false">dev_mask</input>
            <output clear="false">dev_pressure</output>
        </formula>
    </analysis>

    <export>
    </export>
</phyphox>
